      "writtenOn": "2018-12-13T03:11:44Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e \u003e we are not monitoring Vbus level should be using the tTryTimeout instead\n\nYes, but tTryTimeout is 550~1100ms. This means everytime when we connect to a source only device, we will spend this time querying if the port partner supports the sink role. I think it\u0027s too long. So how about using tDRPtry(PD_T_TRY_SRC) and monitoring Vbus level?",
